   "summary": "This report reviews Japanese foreign and domestic developments for October 1939, beginning with Ambassador Joseph C. Grew's address before the America-Japan Society and the strong Japanese press and official reactions. It details diplomatic representations regarding American and third-power rights in China, the settlement at Kulangsu, military operations around Changsha, the severe Japanese defeat at Nomonhan, and foreign policy pronouncements by Foreign Minister Nomura. In domestic matters, the report documents dissension in the Foreign Office over the proposed Trade Ministry, Count Sakai's appointment as Agriculture and Forestry Minister, and severe domestic shortages of coal and electric power. It concludes with lists of despatches and telegrams sent by the Embassy to the Department of State during October 1939.",
