   "summary": "Ambassador Joseph C. Grew transmits Report No. 158 assessing Japanese foreign relations and internal political and economic affairs during November 1939. The report highlights Ambassador Grew's November 4 conversation with Foreign Minister Nomura concerning American rights and the impending expiration of the 1911 commercial treaty, alongside fifty-eight Foreign Office replies to earlier American protests. It also covers the British and French troop reductions in North China, the Japanese military capture of Nanning, Soviet-Japanese diplomatic maneuvering following Foreign Commissar Molotov's speech, negotiations with France and India, an aviation agreement with Thailand, and cabinet reshuffling by Prime Minister Abe.",
